## Key Notes & Data-Quality Flags

- **GWP basis:** The reported Total GWP (**₹1,359.79 cr**) is the statutory Gross Written Premium (statutory/1-n basis), matching the sum of "Grand Total (A+B)" in the Product-wise New+Renewal Business disclosure table — consistent with GWP Growth Rate metrics (37% Health, 112% PA) shown in Note 3.25.

- **Retail health GWP caveat:** The **₹587.39 cr** "Retail Total (A)" figure includes some non-health retail lines (Lifestyle Protection – Accident Care/Critical Care, Saral Suraksha Bima – Personal Accident products), as the Annual Report does not disaggregate a pure "retail health-only" GWP figure. This should be treated as **Retail segment GWP** rather than a health-only figure.

- **PAT is a LOSS** of **₹200.93 crore** for FY23 (vs. a loss of ₹255.96 cr in FY22) — driven primarily by a ₹221.5 cr transfer to the Shareholders' Account for "Excess Expenses of Management (EoM)" over the allowable regulatory limit (Note 3.21), for which the company was granted **regulatory forbearance by IRDAI** (letter dated 6 April 2023), subject to bringing EoM within limits by FY25-26.

- **No IFRS/Ind-AS reporting exists** — ManipalCigna reports solely under Indian GAAP per IRDAI Financial Statement Regulations, 2002. Ind-AS 117 (IFRS 17-aligned) implementation is still at the steering-committee / GAP-study stage (Note 3.30); hence all IFRS-basis rows are blank by design, not omission.

- **Claims / Combined / Commission / EoM ratios** are disclosed only at the **Health segment level** (Note 3.25), not blended company-wide. Given Health is ~98% of total premium (₹1,335.98 cr of ₹1,359.79 cr GWP), these are used as the best available company-representative figures. Cross-check: Net Incurred Claims (₹722.79 cr) ÷ Net Earned Premium (₹1,117.77 cr) = 64.7% ≈ disclosed 65%, confirming consistency.

- **EoM ratio ambiguity:** Two EoM ratios are disclosed — **49%** (vs. Gross Direct Premium, the IRDAI regulatory-standard denominator) and 51% (vs. Net Written Premium). The 49% figure is reported as the primary regulatory metric.

- **Solvency ratio** of **1.56x** (ASM/RSM) is down from 1.68x in FY22 — still above the IRDAI-mandated minimum of 1.50x, but with a narrowing buffer given accumulated losses (debit balance in P&L: ₹1,462.04 cr as of 31 March 2023).

- **Net worth** grew 55% YoY (**₹326.73 cr** FY23 vs ₹210.65 cr FY22) — driven by continued capital infusion (₹316.70 cr fresh equity/premium raised via Preferential Allotment during FY23) rather than internal accruals, since the company remains loss-making.

- **AUM** grew ~35.7% YoY (**₹1,412.16 cr** FY23 vs ₹930.14 cr FY22 combined shareholder + policyholder investments) — consistent with premium growth funding the investment book.

- **Retail health market share** is not disclosed in the statutory Annual Report; this would require IRDAI industry-wide handbook data or a separate investor/analyst estimate, which falls outside the specified source document. Suggest checking the IRDAI Annual Report / Handbook on Indian Insurance Statistics for FY23 industry-wide health market-share data if this metric is needed.</ans>
